OL,3,GNEWSASwinney backs decriminalisation of
OL,4,Adrugs after spike in deaths
OL,5,
OL,6,FFirst Minister John Swinney has
OL,7,Freaffirmed his government's support for
OL,8,Fdecriminalising all drugs for personal
OL,9,Fuse following a spike in drugs deaths.
OL,11,FScotland has retained its grim moniker
OL,12,Fas Europe's drugs deaths capital after
OL,13,Fit was revealed there were 1,133
OL,14,Ffatalities related to illicit drugs
OL,15,Flast year, a rise of 116 (11%) on 2024.
OL,17,FSwinney described the rise as
OL,18,F"unacceptable and intolerable", but
OL,19,Fopposition leaders rounded on the first
OL,20,Fminister, calling his record
OL,21,F"indefensible".
OL,23,APub: 24-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB  Scot NewsC Reg TVF  Weather
